Batch Files
-----------

Three batch files that simplify operation of the FLEXlogic
Prototyping Cable Kit and FLEXlogic Evaluation Board are included 
with the PLDshell Plus/PLDasm software. They are:

SRAM_W.BAT
SRAM_R.BAT
MSG.BAT

SRAM_W.BAT and SRAM_R.BAT

   The SRAM_W.BAT and SRAM_R.BAT files are used to write a JEDEC file 
   to an EPX780 configuration SRAM, and to read an EPX780 configuration
   SRAM into a JEDEC file, respectively. Type the following text
   at the DOS command line to run these batch files:

   SRAM_W name

   SRAM_R name

   where "name" is the basename of the JEDEC file name (without
   the .JED extension).

   Both of these batch files call the executable file PENGN with the
   proper parameters. Refer to the actual batch files for more 
   information.

FLEXlogic Evaluation Kit Message Generator (MSG.BAT)

   The batch file MSG.BAT can be used to easily customize flashing or
   scrolling LCD displays on the FLEXlogic Evaluation Board. Type the
   following text at the DOS command line to run this batch file:

   MSG name

   where "name" becomes the basename of the .PDS PLDasm source
   file.

   The MSG.BAT batch file does the following:

   -  If filename.IN does not exist, it copies the file TEMPLATE.IN
      to filename.IN.

   -  It calls "EDIT filename.IN". An ASCII editor named EDIT must be
      in your path. This is typically the DOS editor, but this
      is not a requirement. The purpose of calling the editor is
      to allow the user to enter their custom message.  See
      "Message Entry" below for more details.

   -  It calls FLS_DFLT to convert filename.IN to filename.PDS.
      FLS_DFLT converts the RAM_DEFAULTS section of filename.IN to 
      a form that is acceptable to PLDasm.

   -  It calls PARPDS, LOCMIN, and, FITENGN to parse, minimize, and
      fit the design.

   -  It calls batch file SRAM_W to write the design to the EPX780
      SRAM.

   -  It returns to the DOS command line. The LCD should now be 
      flashing or scrolling your message.


Entering Messages
-----------------

The RAM_DEFAULTS section of TEMPLATE.IN includes an example of a
scrolling message, which appears as follows:

RAM_DEFAULTS PROM

; #BEGIN FLASH
; #END FLASH
#BEGIN SCROLL
EPX780 10ns FLEXlogic device with SRAM option -- 80MHz System...
#END SCROLL

Either a flashing or scrolling message can be selected, but not both.

When the editor is entered, the scrolling message can be changed, or
it can be deleted and flashing messages can be entered. The entire
scrolling message, up to 120 characters, must be entered on one line.

The following is example shows how to disable the scrolling message and
enter a flashing message:

#BEGIN FLASH
  Good Morning
    World!
#END FLASH
; #BEGIN SCROLL
; EPX780 10ns FLEXlogic device with SRAM option -- 80MHz System...
; #END SCROLL

Up to 16 characters can be entered for each flashing line. The
total number of lines that can be entered depends on their length;
typically 5 to 7 lines can be entered. Lines at the end that don't
fit in the SRAM block are automatically dropped.

Note that the #BEGIN and #END keywords must start in column 1, and
there can be no blank lines between #BEGIN and #END. If you
comment out the unused lines with semicolons as shown above, you
can easily switch between flashing and scrolling displays.

Once a JEDEC file with the desired message has been generated, it
can be re-loaded into the EPX780 with the SRAM_W batch file.

